<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yom Kippur War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1973</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as October War, Ramadan War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yom Kippur War was the surprise offensive of October 1973 in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> sought to recover the lands lost in 1967, crossing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> and storming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golan-heights">Golan Heights</a> on the Day of Atonement. Israel recovered after early reverses and counter-attacked across the canal; the superpowers came to the edge of confrontation; and the shock opened the way to disengagement agreements, the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/us-oil-embargo-against-japan">oil embargo</a>, and ultimately Egypt's peace with Israel.</p></div>
